module examples.cost_forwarding

# Cost-stage golden (plans/M20.md item M) — store-to-load forwarding
# (inventory row 13) against the ordinary L1 path and against a
# compulsory first touch.
#
# WHAT THIS PINS, PREDICTED FROM THE DOCS BEFORE THE CODE WAS RUN
# (`cost::mem`; `[sweep.store_to_load_forwarding]`; `[geometry]`):
#
#   * A store is latency 1 **to the store buffer** (SOG §3.10), and a
#     load of a line a recent store wrote is answered by the buffer
#     before L1D is consulted: `MemLevel::Forwarded`, priced
#     `[sweep.store_to_load_forwarding]`.
#   * The store buffer is `cap_l_each x port_l` = **4** line entries
#     deep, floor-not-fact. A load of a line pushed out of the buffer
#     but still resident falls to `lat_l1d_hit = 4`.
#   * `MemState` is built **per scored block**, so a block's first touch
#     of a line is compulsory and a `Stack` line is charged at its home
#     level `lat_l2 = 11`. A basic block boundary therefore turns a
#     forwarded read into an 11-cycle one with no change to the words.
#
# **Predicted, and it is a null result at the pinned point:** the
# profile pins `store_to_load_forwarding = 4` because its bracket's
# upper bound *is* `lat_l1d_hit` ("forwarding cannot be assumed to beat
# the L1 path", `[sweep.store_to_load_forwarding].source`). So at the
# canonical point `Forwarded` and `L1dHit` cost the **same 4 cycles**,
# and a single-valued golden (decision 1605) cannot separate them. What
# it can separate — and what the three fns below pin — is either of them
# against the **compulsory** path at 11.
#
#   forwarded    every read is answered out of the buffer   (4)
#   l1_path      reads pushed past the 4-entry buffer       (4, via L1D)
#   cross_block  the same read after a branch, fresh state  (11)

# Immediate reuse: each value is stored and read back before four more
# stores can push its line out of the buffer.
pub fn forwarded(a: u64, b: u64) -> u64:
    x: u64 = a +% b
    y: u64 = x +% x
    z: u64 = y +% y
    w: u64 = z +% z
    return w

# Forty-eight slots — six 64 B frame lines — copied in first, and only
# the first eight read back. By the time those reads happen the 4-entry
# store buffer holds only the last lines written, so the line they want
# is long gone from it and they take the L1D path instead.
pub fn l1_path(v: [u64; 48]) -> u64:
    s0: u64 = v[0]
    s1: u64 = v[1]
    s2: u64 = v[2]
    s3: u64 = v[3]
    s4: u64 = v[4]
    s5: u64 = v[5]
    s6: u64 = v[6]
    s7: u64 = v[7]
    return s0 +% s1 +% s2 +% s3 +% s4 +% s5 +% s6 +% s7

# The same reuse, split across a basic block boundary: `MemState` is per
# block, so the reads on the far side of the branch are compulsory.
pub fn cross_block(a: u64, b: u64, take_it: bool) -> u64:
    x: u64 = a +% b
    y: u64 = x +% x
    if take_it:
        return x +% y
    return y +% x
